cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this documentation, please cite it as below. Each linked repository has its own citation and DOI."
title: "maniva. An open commons of evidence, protocols, data and analysis for agricultural research"
abstract: >-
  maniva is an open commons of evidence, protocols, data and analysis for
  agricultural research, built so that people and AI assistants can use them
  together. tricot (triadic comparison of technology options) is its first
  domain. Each layer lives in its own repository with its own skill, licence
  and citation. The knowledge base holds verified cards on the published
  literature. The protocols layer holds standard operating procedures whose
  traits map to the Crop Ontology. The data layer holds harmonized trial data.
  The analysis layer holds curated workflows with decision records, the R
  packages they run on and a template for reproducible projects. One entry
  point routes each question to the layer that answers it, so a user can move
  from a published finding to the trials, protocols and methods behind it in
  one conversation. Further domains, such as climate and household data, join
  as they meet the same standards.
